1.	Identify users – Determine who will use the system.
	2.	Collect requirements – Gather user needs and expectations.
	3.	Identify functional requirements – Decide what features the system must provide.
	4.	Identify non-functional requirements – Define requirements such as performance, security, usability, and reliability.
	5.	Analyze requirements – Check whether the requirements are clear, realistic, and achievable.
	6.	Prioritize requirements – Separate essential features from optional features.
	7.	Document requirements – Prepare a clear requirement specification for development.
